      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CAWBOURNE DOLLAR (1) hasn't been far away here at the last two, finding the frame both times, most recently when second beaten 0.8 lengths (30.23). Safe beginner who draws ideally on the inside. One of the contenders. SONALI (3) could manage only fifth at this track last time but caught the eye when posting a strong 18.82 over 330m at Temora three starts back. Should be in this for a long way. AUNTY MEEKA (4) has been beaten for early speed lately, last time finishing fourth (30.59) in a Grade 4/5 at this track. Has a good record here at this journey. Solid beginner who can clear the tricky draw. A big run wouldn't surprise. CHATTAHOOCHE (8) is going well, finishing in the placings twice in a row. Not beaten far last time when a neck second (18.87) in a Grade 5 at this track.",
